  <prompt>
    Fix the deployed create-on-save eTag mismatch (FR-08). When a document is CREATED on save and then the
    content write follows, the create advances the item eTag — so a follow-up content write that uses the
    PRE-create precondition throws `InvalidOperationException` ("resource changed since caller last read" —
    an eTag-mismatch 500). SEQUENCE create-on-save so the content write uses the POST-CREATE eTag: create
    first, capture the fresh eTag returned by the create, then perform the content write with
    `If-Match: &lt;post-create eTag&gt;`. A genuinely concurrent EXTERNAL edit between create and content-write
    must still yield a clean 412 / ProblemDetails, NOT a 500.

    Modify the `ComposeService` save/create path. SPE writes stay behind `SpeFileStore` (ADR-007) — no
    `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/`. This is an ORDERED save sequence — execute the steps in
    order (`mode="prescriptive"`). Builds on the version-stamped save from 050. Every save-path change carries
    a through-the-wire seam slice (ADR-038; the seam slice is task 054).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 engineer on `ComposeService` + the SPE facade. Understands the SharePoint Embedded
    create-then-write eTag lifecycle: a create returns a fresh eTag that MUST seed the subsequent conditional
    content write, and that a stale precondition is the deployed R3 UAT failure surface.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A create-on-save sequence where the content write uses the POST-create eTag via `If-Match`, so
    create-on-save followed by a content write does NOT throw the eTag-mismatch `InvalidOperationException`;
    and a genuinely concurrent external edit still yields a clean 412 / ProblemDetails, not a 500. SPE writes
    stay behind `SpeFileStore`.
  </goal>

